 ## Background
-The method was developed by Minho Kim et al. to enable real-time isosurface raycasting of FCC datasets using Box-Splines [S1][S2, unofficial]. FCC lattices offer better approximation properties for smooth surfaces but require complex tetrahedral decomposition. Previous methods suffered from performance degradation due to conditional branches and lookup tables [S1]. This optimized version removes these overheads, enabling interactive frame rates [S1]. It is part of a broader effort to utilize FCC/BCC lattices for volume rendering and FEM [S2, unofficial].
